@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+requires "verification.k"
+
+module SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT
+  imports VERIFICATION
+
+  // Fresh reviewer mutation of symbolic claim 1: the first result component is
+  // deliberately one too large. The precondition is satisfiable, for example
+  // NUMBER=5, NEED=6, REMAINING=10; the real result is result(11,4), not
+  // result(12,4).
+  claim <mpy>
+          <k> run(solutionProgram, args(NUMBER, NEED, REMAINING))
+            => result(NUMBER +Int NEED +Int 1, REMAINING -Int NEED)
+          </k>
+        </mpy>
+    requires validInput(NUMBER, NEED, REMAINING)
+             andBool NEED <=Int REMAINING
+endmodule

codex
The adversarial gates are now complete. The proof is body-sensitive and non-vacuous: changing the constructor body produced `result(-1,4)` and a stuck proof, while an independent symbolic off-by-one postcondition built successfully and failed on the exact unmet equality. I’m writing the final seven-stage review now; the only non-fatal limitation is the generated semantics’ globally over-broad `[total]` annotations, which fresh compilation exposed but which no execution path of the pinned program reaches.
apply patch
